Subject: [PATCH v3 2/3] src/lab-process-mail: Thread each revision under its
 first version
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: qwqznozzqsomwsomoqmsmqvmuszmtxtt
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:28:49 +0000

The pass and the mail workflow guide said a revision is a fresh
thread, which no longer matches what format-patch.sh produces. They
now say a revision replies to the first version, so the maintainer
follows a series and its review in one thread, and that format-patch.sh
picks the reply target, so the agent does not pass its own. The list
researcher is told most earlier versions are now in the same thread.
---
